U('incident-review',2,'事故复盘：事实、原因和后续行动','事故报告',[
 ['On Monday, users of the training service were unable to save new reports for approximately twenty minutes. Existing reports remained readable. The problem began shortly after a configuration change, and saving recovered after the team restored the previous configuration. These observations establish the sequence of events, but they do not by themselves explain every part of the failure. The review should distinguish the immediate trigger from the conditions that allowed a single change to interrupt the service.','周一，练习服务的用户大约二十分钟无法保存新报告，已有报告仍可读取。问题发生在一次配置修改后不久，团队恢复旧配置后保存功能恢复。这些观察确定了事件顺序，但本身不能解释故障的所有环节。复盘应区分直接触发因素与使单次修改能够中断服务的条件。'],
 ['The new configuration reduced the number of available connections below what the saving process required during busy periods. The test environment did not reproduce that level of activity, and the deployment check only confirmed that the application had started. It did not attempt to save a report under realistic load. The change passed the checks that existed at the time. Saying that someone “should have tested more” would leave the team without a concrete description of the missing protection.','新配置将可用连接数降低到繁忙时段保存流程所需数量以下。测试环境未复现那种活动水平，部署检查只确认应用已启动，没有尝试在真实负载下保存报告。修改通过了当时已有的检查。仅说某个人“应该多测一些”，无法具体描述缺少了什么保护。'],
 ['The team has agreed on three actions. First, add a post-deployment check that creates and reads a sample report. Second, document the expected connection requirements and reject configurations below that minimum. Third, practise restoring the previous configuration so that recovery does not depend on finding the person who last changed it. Each action has an owner and a review date. Completing these actions should reduce this particular risk, but it would be misleading to claim that no saving failure can happen again.','团队同意三项行动：增加创建并读取示例报告的部署后检查；记录预期连接需求，拒绝低于下限的配置；演练恢复旧配置，避免恢复依赖最后修改它的人。每项都有负责人和审查日期。完成它们应能降低这类风险，但声称保存故障不会再发生会产生误导。'],
 ['Some uncertainty remains. The team has not yet confirmed whether a small number of failed requests were retried successfully by clients. The report should state that limit rather than invent a precise count of lost work. A useful review helps people understand what happened, what is still unknown and what will change. Its purpose is to improve the system, not to produce a story in which one careless person explains everything.','仍有不确定性：团队尚未确认少量失败请求是否被客户端成功重试。报告应说明这一限制，而不是编造精确的工作损失数。有效复盘让人理解发生了什么、哪些尚未知晓，以及将改变什么。目的在于改进系统，而不是将一切归咎于某个粗心的人。']
],[['immediate trigger','直接触发因素','Separate the immediate trigger from underlying conditions.'],['under realistic load','在接近实际的负载下','Test saving under realistic load.'],['concrete action','具体行动','Turn a vague criticism into a concrete action.'],['recovery','恢复','Practise recovery before an incident.'],['uncertainty remains','仍有不确定性','Some uncertainty remains about failed requests.']],[[
 '恢复旧配置后故障消失，作者认为这已经解释所有问题了吗？',['已经完全解释','没有，还需分析系统条件','说明没有发生故障'],1,'首段区分事件顺序与完整解释。'],['为什么“应该多测试”不足以作为行动？',['没有描述具体缺失的保护','测试完全无用','必须只指责个人'],0,'第二段要求指出可执行、可检查的防护改进。'],['尚未确认失败请求的最终结果，应如何写？',['编造精确损失数','说明已知范围和不确定性','完全删除事故报告'],1,'最后一段要求保留不确定性。']
],{task:'为一个虚构的软件故障写复盘摘要。',audience:'需要改进系统的团队',length:'180～250 词',requirements:['分开写影响、观察和解释','提出两项有负责人及复查时间的具体行动','明确一个尚未证实的问题，避免保证永不复发'],starter:'Impact and observations:\nContributing conditions:\nActions and open questions:',model:'On Monday, users could read existing reports but could not save new ones for about twenty minutes. Saving recovered after the team restored the previous configuration. This links the incident to the configuration change, but the review also identified weaknesses in testing and recovery preparation.\n\nThe new connection limit was too low for busy periods. Our test environment did not reproduce that activity, and the deployment check only verified that the application started. It never attempted a realistic save operation. We should improve those checks rather than treat “test more carefully” as a complete action.\n\nLena will add a post-deployment check that creates and reads a sample report, with a review scheduled for next Wednesday. Omar will document the minimum connection requirement and add configuration validation before the next release. We will also practise restoring the previous configuration without relying on one particular person.\n\nWe have not confirmed whether all failed requests were later retried successfully, so we cannot yet give a precise count of lost work. The proposed actions should reduce this failure mode. They do not justify a promise that saving can never fail again. We will track their completion and review their effectiveness after deployment.'});
U('migration-plan',2,'迁移计划为何需要退出条件','项目方案',[
 ['The team wants to move its internal help centre to a new platform. The current platform is difficult to search, but it contains links used in support replies, onboarding documents and saved bookmarks. A successful migration therefore involves more than copying article text. Readers need to reach the right information, existing links need a deliberate treatment, and editors need to know where future changes belong. A visually complete new site could still be an incomplete migration if those relationships are ignored.','团队想把内部帮助中心迁到新平台。旧平台难以搜索，却有大量链接用于支持回复、入职文档和书签。因此成功迁移不只是复制文章：读者要能找到正确信息，旧链接要妥善处理，编辑要知道以后在哪里更新。忽略这些关系，即使新站外观完整，迁移仍可能不完整。'],
 ['I propose beginning with a small group of frequently used articles. For each article, record its owner, existing address, replacement address and any information that needs correction. Test the new navigation with people who did not perform the migration. If we explain every confusing label during the test, we will learn little about whether the site works independently. We should also check a sample of old links from real support templates rather than only clicking through the new home page.','我建议先迁一小组常用文章。每篇记录负责人、原地址、新地址和待修正内容。请未参与迁移的人测试导航；如果测试时解释每个困惑标签，就无法了解网站能否独立工作。也应抽查真实支持模板中的旧链接，而不是只浏览新首页。'],
 ['During the trial, the old help centre should remain available. However, keeping both sites editable indefinitely would create two competing versions. We need a short, explicit transition period and a rule for where updates are made. The plan should name the person who can stop the migration if important links fail or editors cannot complete their work. Stopping a trial is not evidence that the entire idea is wrong; it may simply prevent a known problem from reaching more readers.','试用期间保留旧帮助中心。但若无限期让两站都可编辑，会形成相互竞争的版本。需要明确而短暂的过渡期及更新位置规则。计划应指定在重要链接失效或编辑无法工作时有权暂停迁移的人。停止试用不代表整个构想错误，也可能是在防止已知问题影响更多读者。'],
 ['Before expanding, agree on exit criteria: essential links resolve correctly, article owners can publish updates, and trial readers can complete the selected tasks without extra guidance. These criteria should be checked, not assumed from the number of copied pages. After the trial, we can decide whether to continue, revise the approach or remain on the old platform temporarily. The schedule should support that decision rather than make the trial an irreversible formality.','扩大迁移前，应约定完成试用的标准：重要链接正确、负责人可发布更新、试读者无需额外指导即可完成所选任务。标准需要核验，不能根据复制页数推断。试用后再决定继续、调整还是暂留旧平台。进度表应支持这种决策，而不是让试用变成不可逆的形式流程。']
],[['deliberate treatment','有意识的处理','Existing links need deliberate treatment.'],['transition period','过渡期','Agree on a short transition period.'],['competing versions','相互竞争的版本','Avoid maintaining competing versions.'],['exit criteria','完成或退出阶段的标准','Check the exit criteria before expanding.'],['irreversible','不可逆的','The trial should not be an irreversible formality.']],[[
 '复制完全部文章就一定迁移成功了吗？',['一定','不一定，还涉及链接、导航和更新流程','只需要换背景色'],1,'第一段强调文字复制之外的关系。'],['为什么不能长期允许两站同时编辑？',['会产生相互竞争的版本','因为旧文章必须立即销毁','因为任何试用都不允许撤回'],0,'第三段解释了双版本风险。'],['扩大迁移前应依据什么判断？',['复制页数最多','预先约定且已核验的标准','是否已经宣布发布日期'],1,'最后一段要求检查任务、链接和发布能力。']
],{task:'为一个小型文档迁移写试点方案。',audience:'文档维护者和项目负责人',length:'180～250 词',requirements:['说明迁移范围和旧链接处理','定义过渡期的编辑规则与暂停条件','写出可核验的试点完成标准'],starter:'The first trial will cover…\nDuring the transition,…\nWe will expand only when…',model:'The first trial will cover the ten help articles most often used by the support team. We will record each article’s owner, old address, new address and any content that needs correction. The goal is to preserve useful routes to information, not simply to copy pages.\n\nDuring a two-week transition, the old site will remain readable. Updates to trial articles will be made on the new platform, and their old pages will clearly direct readers to the replacement. We will not keep two editable copies indefinitely. The documentation lead can pause the trial if essential links fail or article owners cannot publish necessary changes.\n\nWe will ask colleagues who did not perform the migration to complete several common tasks. We should observe their difficulties before explaining the interface. We will also test old links taken from actual support templates.\n\nWe will expand only when essential links work, owners can update their articles and trial readers can complete the chosen tasks without extra guidance. If those conditions are not met, we will revise the approach or remain on the old platform temporarily. The number of copied pages will be tracked, but it will not be our only measure of completion.'});
U('async-message',2,'异步沟通：让别人不必追问','工作方式',[
 ['A useful written update should allow someone to understand the situation without first arranging a conversation. This does not mean that every message must be long. It means that the message should contain the information needed for its purpose: what changed, why the recipient is involved, what action is requested and when a response would be useful. A short message that omits the actual question can create more work than a slightly longer one that makes the decision clear.','有效的书面更新应让对方不必先约谈就能理解情况。这不意味着每条消息都要很长，而是要包含实现目的所需的信息：变化、对方为何相关、要求什么行动，以及何时答复有用。短消息若省略真正问题，可能比稍长但明确决策的消息制造更多工作。'],
 ['Consider the message “Can we change the form?” The reader does not know which form, what is wrong with it or whether the sender needs permission, technical advice or a review. A more useful version would identify the form, explain the observed problem and propose a specific change. It would also state what remains uncertain. If a sample request shows that users misunderstand a field, include that example with personal details removed instead of merely saying that the form is confusing.','例如“我们能改表单吗？”读者不知道哪个表单、哪里有问题，也不知道发信者需要许可、技术建议还是审查。更有用的版本会指出表单、解释观察到的问题、提出具体改法，并说明尚不确定的部分。如果示例申请表明用户误解某字段，应移除个人信息后提供例子，而不只是说表单令人困惑。'],
 ['Timing matters too. “Please reply today” is clearer than “as soon as possible”, but it still helps to explain why that date matters. If no reply arrives, what will happen? For a reversible design choice, the sender might proceed with a stated default. For an important decision that requires approval, silence should not be treated as permission. The message needs to make that difference visible so that the recipient does not have to guess the consequences of waiting.','时间也重要。“请今天回复”比“尽快”清楚，但最好还说明日期为何重要。没有回复会怎样？对于可逆设计选择，发信者可能按已说明的默认方案继续；对于需要批准的重要决策，沉默不应视为许可。消息要明确区别，让收件人不必猜测等待的后果。'],
 ['Written communication still has limits. If several replies reveal different assumptions about the same term, a short conversation may resolve them faster. Afterwards, record the decision and its reasons so that people who were not present can follow the work. The aim is not to avoid every conversation. It is to reduce unnecessary dependence on immediate availability while keeping decisions understandable and accountable.','书面沟通仍有限制。如果几轮回复暴露了对同一术语的不同假设，短谈可能更快解决。之后应记录决定和理由，让未在场的人也能跟进。目标不是避免所有对话，而是减少对即时在线的无谓依赖，同时让决策可理解、有记录可查。']
],[['recipient','收件人；接收者','Tell the recipient what action is needed.'],['observed problem','观察到的问题','Describe the observed problem.'],['reversible choice','可逆的选择','A reversible choice may allow a stated default.'],['proceed with','按……继续','We will proceed with the proposed layout.'],['immediate availability','即时可联系状态','Reduce dependence on immediate availability.']],[[
 '作者主张每条消息都写得越长越好吗？',['是','不是，应包含实现目的所需的信息','消息应只剩一个问号'],1,'首段区分篇幅与信息是否足够。'],['什么情况下不能把沉默当许可？',['重要且需要批准的决策','已经约定可逆默认方案时','任何消息都必须默许'],0,'第三段明确区别可逆默认选择与正式批准。'],['短谈解决歧义后还应做什么？',['只靠参与者记忆','记录决定及理由','删除原有任务'],1,'末段强调让未在场者也能理解。']
],{task:'把“这个设置能不能改一下？”改写为一封能独立理解的请求。',audience:'负责作出决定的同事',length:'180～240 词',requirements:['补充具体设置、问题和证据','提出方案及未确定因素','说明答复时间、原因，以及未获批准时如何处理'],starter:'I would like to propose…\nThe problem we observed is…\nCould you confirm… by…?',model:'I would like to propose changing the default notification setting for new training accounts. At present, every sample event produces a desktop alert. During the last onboarding session, two participants said they could not follow the instructions because the alerts kept covering the relevant controls. I have attached a screenshot using sample data.\n\nMy proposal is to keep messages in the inbox but disable desktop previews by default during onboarding. Users would still be able to enable them afterwards. I have not checked whether this would affect users who depend on immediate alerts, so I would like your input before making the change.\n\nCould you confirm by Thursday afternoon whether we should test this with the next small onboarding group? That timing would allow us to update the instructions before Friday. I am requesting approval for the trial, not for a permanent change across all accounts.\n\nIf I do not receive approval, I will keep the current setting and note the issue in the session guide. If the terms “alert” and “message” mean different things to us, I can arrange a short discussion and record the resulting decision afterwards.'});
U('test-evidence',2,'“测试通过”究竟证明了多少','技术论证',[
 ['A team reports that its new search feature is reliable because all tests passed. That statement may be encouraging, but its meaning depends on what the tests actually covered. A test suite is a set of observations under selected conditions. It can provide strong evidence about those conditions without proving that every possible input, device or network state will behave correctly. Readers should ask which claim is being supported rather than treating “tested” as a complete explanation.','团队说新搜索功能可靠，因为所有测试都通过了。这或许令人鼓舞，但含义取决于测试具体覆盖什么。测试集是在选定条件下的一组观察，能为这些条件提供有力证据，却不能证明所有输入、设备和网络状态都会正确运行。读者应问证据支持哪个结论，而不是把“测过了”当成完整解释。'],
 ['Suppose the tests used a small collection of short project names on a fast local connection. They may show that matching and sorting work for that collection. They do not directly show how the feature performs with thousands of long names or when the remote service responds slowly. This does not make the tests worthless. It identifies the boundary between the evidence already available and the questions that still need investigation. That boundary should be visible in the report.','假设测试使用高速本地连接下的一小组短项目名，可能证明这组数据的匹配和排序正确，但不能直接证明数千个长名称或远程服务缓慢时的表现。这并不让测试变得毫无价值，而是在区分已有证据与待调查的问题。报告应明确这个边界。'],
 ['A stronger update would describe the important cases checked, explain why they matter and name the remaining risks. It might say that normal matching, empty queries and unavailable-service messages have been tested, while large datasets still need review. If the team claims an improvement over the previous version, the comparison should use a similar task and environment. A faster result from an easier test does not, by itself, demonstrate that the new version is faster for users.','更有力的更新会描述重要测试用例、解释其意义并指出剩余风险。例如说明已测试正常匹配、空查询和服务不可用提示，大数据集仍待检查。如果声称比旧版改善，对比应使用相似任务和环境。更简单测试中的更快结果，本身不能证明用户使用时新版更快。'],
 ['This way of writing is useful outside software too. A trial lesson, a product demonstration or a survey can all provide evidence with limits. Clear limits make a claim easier to assess; they do not automatically weaken it. The responsible question is not “Can you prove everything?” but “Does this evidence justify the decision we are about to make, and what uncertainty are we accepting?”','这种写法也适用于软件之外：试课、产品演示和调查都能提供有限证据。明确限制让结论更易评估，并不自动削弱它。负责任的问题不是“能证明一切吗”，而是“证据是否足以支持当前决策，我们接受了哪些不确定性”。']
],[['test coverage','测试覆盖范围','Describe the test coverage.'],['under selected conditions','在选定条件下','The observation holds under selected conditions.'],['worthless','毫无价值的','Limited evidence is not necessarily worthless.'],['by itself','单独凭这一点','A faster result does not by itself prove the claim.'],['justify a decision','为决策提供充分依据','Does the evidence justify this decision?']],[[
 '作者如何看待有限范围的测试？',['毫无价值','有价值，但结论应符合覆盖范围','能证明一切永不出错'],1,'第二段明确说并非 worthless。'],['比较新旧版本速度时，应注意什么？',['使用相似任务和环境','新版测试越简单越好','只比较界面颜色'],0,'第三段要求可比较的条件。'],['明确证据限制的作用是什么？',['使结论无法使用','让读者更容易评估结论和决策','自动证明产品失败'],1,'最后一段解释了限制说明的价值。']
],{task:'写一份搜索功能验证结果，避免把有限测试写成全面保证。',audience:'决定是否进行小范围试用的负责人',length:'180～240 词',requirements:['写出已测条件和观察结果','明确至少两项未覆盖情形','给出与证据相称的下一步建议'],starter:'The current tests cover…\nThey do not yet establish…\nBased on this evidence,…',model:'The current tests cover normal matching, empty search queries and the message shown when the service is unavailable. We used a small set of sample project names on a fast local connection. All of these cases passed, and the results support a limited trial using similar data.\n\nThey do not yet establish acceptable performance for large collections of long names. We also have not checked slow or interrupted remote connections on the devices used by the support team. These are gaps in the current evidence, not proof that those situations will fail. We should describe them clearly rather than claim that the search feature is reliable under all conditions.\n\nBased on this evidence, I recommend a small internal trial while we prepare the remaining checks. The trial should use sample data and include a clear way to report confusing results. Before making a speed claim, we should compare the old and new versions using the same task, dataset and environment.\n\nI will record the conditions and results of the additional checks. We can then decide whether the evidence supports a wider release and which uncertainties still need to be accepted or reduced.'});
U('accessible-instructions',2,'说明清楚，也要让不同读者能用','文档设计',[
 ['A support article can be accurate and still be difficult to use. It may rely on a screenshot that is too small, describe a button only by its colour or assume that every reader uses a mouse. These choices create obstacles unrelated to the actual task. Improving the article does not always require more technical detail. Often it requires a clearer connection between what the reader wants to do and the controls or information needed to do it.','支持文章可以准确，却仍然难用。它可能依赖太小的截图、只按颜色描述按钮，或假定所有人都用鼠标。这些选择制造了与任务本身无关的障碍。改进不一定需要更多技术细节，往往需要更清楚地连接读者目标与所需控件或信息。'],
 ['For example, “click the green button on the right” may fail when the interface changes, the window becomes narrow or the reader cannot distinguish that colour. Naming the control as well as explaining its purpose gives the reader another way to identify it. Screenshots can support the instructions, but the essential steps should also appear in text. If the application offers a documented keyboard route, include it where it helps people perform the task rather than presenting it as a hidden advanced trick.','例如“点击右边绿色按钮”，在界面变动、窗口变窄或读者无法辨别颜色时可能失效。写出控件名称并解释用途，能提供另一种识别方式。截图可以辅助，但关键步骤也应以文字呈现。如果应用有文档明确的键盘操作路径，可在有助于任务时加入，而不是当作隐藏的高级技巧。'],
 ['Clear structure also matters. Descriptive headings help readers find the relevant section without reading every paragraph. A warning should appear before the action that creates the risk, not several screens below it. Link text should explain where a link leads instead of repeating “click here” throughout the article. These changes can help people using assistive technology, but they also benefit readers scanning a page while trying to solve an urgent problem.','清晰结构也重要。描述性标题让读者无需读完所有段落就能找到相关部分。警告应放在危险操作之前，而不是几屏之后。链接文字应解释去向，而不是整篇重复“点这里”。这些改动能帮助辅助技术使用者，也有利于急着解决问题、快速浏览页面的人。'],
 ['No checklist can replace checking the actual experience. Ask people with different ways of using the product to try important tasks, and record where the instructions fail them. Do not describe an article as accessible merely because it contains alternative text or passes one automated check. Those are useful steps, but the stronger question is whether people can understand the instructions and complete the task with the tools they use.','没有清单能代替真实体验检查。让使用方式不同的人尝试重要任务，并记录说明在哪里没能帮到他们。不要仅因为有替代文本或通过一项自动检查，就宣称文章具备完整可访问性。那些步骤有用，但更关键的是，人们能否用自己的工具理解说明并完成任务。']
],[['unrelated to','与……无关','The obstacle is unrelated to the task.'],['distinguish','辨别','Some readers cannot distinguish the colours.'],['essential step','关键步骤','Put essential steps in text.'],['descriptive heading','描述性标题','Use descriptive headings.'],['assistive technology','辅助技术','Test with assistive technology where appropriate.']],[[
 '为什么只写“右边绿色按钮”不够稳妥？',['颜色、布局或辨色能力可能不同','因为所有按钮都不能用','因为文字必须更长'],0,'第二段列出多个失效条件。'],['重要警告应放在哪里？',['风险操作之前','文章最下面','只放截图文件名里'],0,'第三段强调警告与动作的先后关系。'],['通过一项自动检查能证明所有读者都能完成任务吗？',['能','不能，还要检查实际体验','能替代一切试用'],1,'最后一段区分有用检查与完整体验。']
],{task:'为一篇难用的操作指南提出改进建议。',audience:'文档维护者',length:'180～240 词',requirements:['指出具体障碍及其影响','提出控件命名、文本步骤和结构改进','给出实际验证方式，避免绝对可访问性承诺'],starter:'The current guide assumes…\nI suggest…\nWe should verify…',model:'The current guide assumes that readers can identify controls by colour and use a mouse. Its first instruction says “click the green button on the right”, but the button moves when the window is narrow. The only complete explanation is inside a screenshot, so readers who cannot use that image have little help.\n\nI suggest naming the control and explaining its purpose. Essential steps should be written in text, with screenshots used as supporting information. Where the product documents a keyboard route, we should include it beside the relevant action. The warning about replacing a file should appear before the replacement step, and descriptive headings should separate setup from troubleshooting.\n\nWe should verify the revised guide with people who use the product in different ways. Ask them to complete the same important task and observe where they pause or need additional explanation. Automated checks can identify some issues, but passing one check will not prove that everyone can use the article.\n\nThe immediate goal is to remove specific, observed obstacles and confirm that the instructions work with the tools readers actually use. We can then record remaining problems and improve the guide further.'});
U('privacy-choice',2,'设置里的默认值，也是一种选择','产品分析',[
 ['A product asks users whether they want to share usage information to help improve the service. The choice appears simple, but a useful explanation must answer several questions. What information is collected? Is it linked to an account? Does it include the contents of documents or only events such as opening a feature? Can the user change the choice later? A short label such as “help us improve” does not answer these questions by itself.','产品询问用户是否愿意分享使用信息来改进服务。选择看似简单，但有用的解释必须回答几个问题：收集什么，是否与账户关联，是否包含文档内容还是只含打开功能等事件，以后能否更改？“帮助我们改进”这种简短标签本身并未回答。'],
 ['In our proposed interface, optional usage sharing would be off for a new account. The explanation would give concrete examples of included and excluded data, with a link to more detail. This proposal does not mean that the application sends no information when sharing is off. Signing in, synchronising a document or reporting a crash may involve separate data flows. The interface should distinguish those activities instead of suggesting that one switch controls every network request.','我们的界面提案让新账户的可选使用信息分享默认关闭。说明会具体举例哪些数据包括、哪些不包括，并链接更多细节。这不意味着关闭后应用完全不发送信息：登录、同步文档、报告崩溃可能涉及独立数据流。界面应区分这些活动，不能暗示一个开关控制所有网络请求。'],
 ['Changing a setting also raises a timing question. Does turning sharing off stop future collection only, or does it remove information already stored? If removal requires another action, that should be stated near the setting. Readers should not have to infer the difference from a long policy document. Likewise, turning sharing on should not be described as necessary for basic editing if editing works without it. A choice becomes less meaningful when the explanation exaggerates the cost of refusing it.','修改设置还涉及时间：关闭分享只停止以后收集，还是也删除已存信息？如果删除需要另一项操作，应在设置旁说明，而不是让读者从长政策文件中猜测。同样，如果基础编辑无需分享就能工作，就不应将打开分享描述为编辑必需。夸大拒绝的代价会让选择失去意义。'],
 ['The team should review the explanation against the actual implementation before release. Clear writing cannot compensate for a control that does something different from its label. We should also test whether users understand what changes when they make a choice. The aim is not to make everyone choose the same option. It is to give people a decision whose scope and consequences they can understand.','发布前，团队应将说明与实际实现对照。控件行为若不同于标签，再清楚的文字也无法弥补。还要测试用户是否理解作出选择后会改变什么。目标不是让所有人选同一个选项，而是让人能理解决策的范围和后果。']
],[['usage information','使用信息','Explain which usage information is collected.'],['linked to','与……关联','Is the event linked to an account?'],['excluded data','被排除的数据','Give examples of included and excluded data.'],['future collection','未来的数据收集','The switch stops future collection.'],['scope and consequences','范围与后果','Explain the scope and consequences of the choice.']],[[
 '关闭可选分享，是否意味着应用绝不发送任何数据？',['意味着','不意味着，登录同步等可能有独立数据流','意味着不能再使用编辑器'],1,'第二段明确限制该开关的范围。'],['停止未来收集与删除过去数据是同一件事吗？',['是','不一定，需要分别说明','文字越短越一定相同'],1,'第三段提出时间与范围的区分。'],['发布前应核对什么？',['文案是否符合实际实现','默认开启是否让按钮更好看','是否每个人都选一样'],0,'最后一段强调标签与行为一致。']
],{task:'为一个可选使用数据开关撰写说明与设计理由。',audience:'产品团队',length:'180～240 词',requirements:['定义收集范围并举例','区分其他必要数据流与过去数据删除','说明如何核对实现和测试理解'],starter:'The setting should explain…\nTurning it off would…\nBefore release,…',model:'The setting should explain the optional usage information we collect, rather than simply asking users to help improve the product. I propose keeping it off for new accounts and giving concrete examples near the switch. Before writing the final text, we need to confirm whether events are linked to accounts and whether document contents are excluded.\n\nTurning optional sharing off should not be described as stopping every network request. Signing in and synchronising documents involve separate activities that need their own explanations. We must also state whether the switch stops future collection only. If removing previously stored information requires another action, provide a clear route to that action.\n\nThe wording should not imply that optional sharing is necessary for basic editing if that is not true. Users should be able to understand the consequences of declining without reading an exaggerated warning.\n\nBefore release, we should check the explanation against the actual data flows and ask trial users what they expect the switch to do. The goal is not a particular acceptance rate. It is a choice whose scope, limits and consequences match both the implementation and the reader’s understanding.'});
